new:
  "title": "Speculative Conditional Hypotheses: amennyiben, abban az esetben, ha; azzal a feltétellel, hogy",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Conditions You Know",
      "content": "You know *amennyiben* ('if, in the event that') and *abban az esetben, ha* ('in the event that') from B2 Unit 13: both state a condition more formally than plain *ha*, and the main clause often continues with *úgy* ('then'). You also know *azzal a feltétellel, hogy* ('on the condition that') from B2 Unit 14, where *azzal* points ahead to the *hogy* clause. This lesson uses them to talk about forecasts and tests: what must be true before a new machine can start."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Real and Doubtful Conditions",
      "content": "A condition that can really come true takes the plain present: *Amennyiben a kísérlet sikerül, úgy ...* For a condition you doubt, use the conditional you know (-na/-ne): *Abban az esetben, ha a gép elromlana, ...* The new words of the lesson name the things such a text talks about: *feltétel* (condition), *hipotézis*, *előrejelzés* (forecast) and *kísérlet* (experiment)."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Conditions for Forecasts and Tests",
      "rows": [
        [
          "amennyiben ..., úgy ...",
          "Amennyiben a gép jól működik, úgy elkezdhetjük a kísérletet. (If the machine works well, we can begin the experiment.)"
        ],
        [
          "abban az esetben, ha ...",
          "Abban az esetben, ha a gép elromlana, a tudósok leállítanák a kísérletet. (In the event that the machine broke down, the scientists would stop the experiment.)"
        ],
        [
          "azzal a feltétellel, hogy ...",
          "A tudós azzal a feltétellel dolgozik, hogy a gép biztonságos. (The scientist works on the condition that the machine is safe.)"
        ],
        [
          "akkor ..., ha ...",
          "A hipotézis akkor marad érvényes, ha az új adatok is igazolják. (The hypothesis stays valid if the new data confirm it too.)"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "title": "Authentic B2 Examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Amennyiben a gép jól működik, úgy a tudósok elkezdhetik a kísérletet.",
          "english": "If the machine works well, the scientists can begin the experiment."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "A kísérletet azzal a feltétellel engedélyezték, hogy a tudósok ellenőrzik az eredményt.",
          "english": "The experiment was approved on the condition that the scientists check the result."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Abban az esetben, ha az előrejelzés igaz, a gyárak jövőre új gépeket vásárolnak.",
          "english": "In the event that the forecast is true, the factories will buy new machines next year."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "A hipotézis akkor marad érvényes, ha az új adatok is igazolják.",
          "english": "The hypothesis stays valid if the new data confirm it too."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "title": "B2 Stylistic Notice",
      "content": "Plain *ha* is still the everyday word. *Amennyiben* and *abban az esetben, ha* sound careful and official: use them when you state a condition for a forecast or a test."
    }
  ]
}

